! A frame around a word, where the word arrives after the frame. `...` in the
! second column is a held stroke: its keys are read and the text they read is
! not written yet. A frame reports under its own outline, on the line after the
! word it went around.
!
! The frames are in `tests/dicts/frames.xfst`, the words in `words.dict`.

! ---- the ordinary case
!buffer
TPR
HAOEUR

! Two frames in a row: the second one gets the word and the first is gone.
!buffer
TPR
TKPW
KAT

! ---- what a frame is shown
! One word or two, and the frame that reads one does not match two at all.
!buffer
PW
TWA
!buffer
TPR
TWA

! The window is the unit's own words, so a frame cannot reach back over text
! that was already there.
!buffer already written
TPR
KAT

! ---- units that are not a word
! A record that joins into the word before it wrote no word of its own, and a
! command wrote nothing at all. The frame waits through both.
!buffer word
TPR
SKWR
PHRO
HAOEUR

! A command right after the frame, with a word already in the buffer. What the
! frame waits for is the words written since its keys, and the command wrote
! none, so the word that was already there is not its window.
!buffer word
TPR
PHRO
KAT

! ---- a longer match over the frame's own stroke
! The frame's stroke turns out to be the first half of an entry in another
! dictionary, so the frame never happened.
!buffer
TPR
KAT
KAT

! ---- undo
! Taking the word back leaves the frame waiting again, because the frame the
! stroke found is what the mark puts back.
!buffer
TKPW
HAOEUR
!undo
KAT

! ---- a record that follows the next unit rather than reading it
! `[AFTER]`: the tail is stroked first and the host joins it to the word the next
! unit writes. Nothing is read, so there is no window and no glyph in the record,
! and the stroke is an ordinary match rather than a held one: what waits is the
! tail, and the body writes at once.
!buffer
KWRS
KAT

! It waits through a unit that wrote nothing, as a frame does.
!buffer
KWRS
PHRO
KAT

! A body and a tail: the body writes now and the tail waits for the word.
!buffer
KWRT
KAT

! The same join a frame waits through, under a tail. A tail waits for text rather
! than for a word, because it follows the text rather than reading it, so a
! record that joined into the word before it is the unit it wanted.
!buffer word
KWRT
SKWR

! A longer match over the held stroke, so the record never lands.
!buffer
KWRS
KAT

! Undo puts the held tail back, because the mark carries it.
!buffer
KWRS
HAOEUR
!undo
KAT
